[]{#sec:intro label="sec:intro"}

The space of three-dimensional superconformal field theories is vast and only partially explored. Many superconformal field theories can be defined as the IR fixed point of supersymmetric gauge theories coupled to matter. The inclusion of Chern-Simons couplings gives a large variety of IR fixed points, as the CS coupling does not flow. Furthermore, in supersymmetric CS theories coupled to matter, the CS coupling controls the strength of several interaction terms in the Lagrangian.

